#: ../../expand_tooluniverse/async_tools_guide.rst:572
#: 21273ff2689e4b59a784f726a66b1d3b
msgid ""
"**Keep submit_job lightweight** - Just submit and return ID **Handle all "
"status cases** - completed, failed, running, unknown **Validate inputs "
"early** - Fail fast in submit_job **Use appropriate intervals** - 10-30s "
"for most APIs **Set realistic timeouts** - Consider actual job duration "
"**Return progress when available** - Better UX **Use helper methods** - "
"Keep methods focused and clean **Test with mocks first** - Don't hit real"
" APIs in unit tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../expand_tooluniverse/async_tools_guide.rst:582
#: 9bb2476b98d64f6a9ae11f72dee3a0ce
msgid "Don'ts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../expand_tooluniverse/async_tools_guide.rst:584
#: 845bcfd6b9d041bf95bc91fe622e4c9f
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Don't do work in submit_job** - Just submit to external service **Don't"
" block in check_status** - Should be a quick status check **Don't poll "
"too frequently** - Respect API rate limits (<10s is usually too much) "
"**Don't set infinite timeouts** - Always have max_duration **Don't "
"swallow errors** - Return {\"error\": \"...\"} or raise exception **Don't"
" use time.sleep()** - Use asyncio.sleep() or let base class handle it "
"**Don't return raw API responses** - Format consistently"
msgstr ""

